course: dictionary
lesson: 10236
title: Together: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Together has several meanings, and the sentence around it shows which one you need. «We play together» means with each other. «Glue the pieces together» means joined into one thing. Ask yourself: are people or things side by side, or are they being joined?
explain: Together can also mean added up. «Together they have 15» means the total of everything they have is 15. The formal word combined means the same kind of thing: all put into one total.
explain: Together is also part of useful phrases: put together, all together, get together, work together, together with. A get-together is a small party. When you meet a phrase, think about what each word does, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Exam writers often use other words for together, such as combined, jointly, collectively and in aggregate. When you see one of these, it is a clue that the sentence means together in a formal way.
fact: Together means with each other, in one place, or at the same time.
fact: Together can mean joined into one group or one thing, as in «Glue the pieces together».
fact: Together can mean added up: «Together they have 15» means the total of all of them is 15.
fact: «Super glue sticks skin together in seconds, so only an adult uses it.»
fact: «A newborn baby has more bones than an adult, because some bones join together as we grow.»
exercise: «Super glue sticks skin together in seconds.» What does together mean here? | With each other, playing a game | Far apart | *Joined into one | Added up to a total
exercise: «Together they have 15.» What does together mean here? | Side by side at school | Joined into one thing | Lost in a crowd | *Added up
exercise: Nadia says a get-together is a tidy room. What does a get-together really mean? | A broken toy | A tidy room | A long journey | *A small party
test: «Water and electricity are dangerous together.» What does together mean here? | Far apart from each other | *When they are in contact with each other | Quietly, one at a time | Added up to a total
test: Which formal word can replace together in an exam sentence? | Slowly | *Collectively | Quickly | Loudly
exam: «Loud and warm can go together.» What does together mean here? | Joined into one thing | Far apart | Added up | *Can happen at the same time
